%description:

Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass:nocc -- without congestion control, the first flight is the whole window of the peer.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the NED type of the algorithm of each connection";
TcpNoCongestionControl has no congestion window.

The classes: the nine algorithms of the package inet.transportlayer.tcp.flavours (TcpNewReno is
the default, TcpReno the value of LegacyTcp, TcpCubic of LinuxTcp), qualified-alias (a
qualified NED type name), unknown (a name without a NED type: an error) and socket-override
(the open command of a socket selects another algorithm). Each test of an algorithm checks a
behavior that none of the other eight algorithms shows. The code:
TcpConnection::createTcpAlgorithm() and the classes of the algorithms. This test separates TcpNoCongestionControl: the seven algorithms with congestion control
send an initial window of three segments, and DumbTcp measures no round trip, so it gives no
signal rto.

Host under test: host1, which sends 100000 bytes; the round trip is 40 ms and the window of
host2 is 65535 bytes. Observation: level 1, more than 20 data segments before the first ACK
of data; level 2, then a value of the signal rto.

%# parameter: Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# class: nocc
%# value: "TcpNoCongestionControl"
%# key: *.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpAlgorithmClassNoCongestionControl")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .meanwhile(anyNumberOfTimes(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                                        .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
                                        .captureCount("flight")
                                        .within(2.0)))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && tcp.ackBit == true && tcp.ackNo > {isn} + 1")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("{flight} > 20")
             .describe("the first ACK of data, after more than 20 data segments")
             .within(1.0))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("rto").describe("a value of the RTO, from a measurement").within(1.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpAlgorithmClassNoCongestionControl compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "TcpNoCongestionControl"    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 100000B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpAlgorithmClassNoCongestionControl: PASS
